{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/staffSize","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails\/staffsize"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLStaffDetailsV9staffSizeAA0cF0VSgvp","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"staffSize"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStaffSizeV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStaffSize"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"staffSize"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"How large a staff space is on this staff.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"staffSize"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStaffSizeV","text":"MXLStaffSize"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<staff-size>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails/staffSize":{"title":"staffSize","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"staffSize"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStaffSizeV","text":"MXLStaffSize"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails\/staffsize","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/staffSize","abstract":[{"text":"How large a staff space is on this staff.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffSize":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The staff-size element indicates how large a staff space is on this staff, expressed as a percentage of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"work’s default scaling. Values less than 100 make the staff space smaller while values over 100 make the staff","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"space larger. A staff-type of cue, ossia, or editorial implies a staff-size of less than 100, but the exact","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value is implementation-dependent unless specified here. Staff size affects staff height only, not the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relationship of the staff to the left and right margins.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffsize","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffSize"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLStaffSize","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffSize"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-details element is used to indicate different types of staves. The optional number attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies the staff number from top to bottom on the system, as with clef. The print-object attribute is used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to indicate when a staff is not printed in a part, usually in large scores where empty parts are omitted. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is yes by default. If print-spacing is yes while print-object is no, the score is printed in cutaway format"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where vertical space is left for the empty part."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffDetails"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLStaffDetails","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffDetails"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"}}}